I take my mobile phone and call the doctor's practice.
A woman answers the phone.
"Good morning, Doctor Weber's practice," the receptionist says.
"How can I help you?"
"Good morning, my name is Maya Flores," I answer.
"I do not feel good at all today."
"I need an appointment because I am sick."
"Do you have a fever?" she asks.
"No, but my throat hurts a lot," I say.
"And I have to come today because my ears hurt now too."
The receptionist types quietly on her keyboard.
"We still have an appointment free this morning," she then says.
"Can you come at half past ten?"
I look at the clock on my mobile phone.
It is only shortly after nine.
"Yes, half past ten fits well," I answer.
"Good, Frau Flores," she says.
"You should bring your insurance card with you."
"I will do that, see you later," I say and hang up.
